      420.08,
      245.99
    ],
    "reading_order": 9,
    "text": "In  ABC, the side BC is the opposite side in relation to the known  A. Now,\nwhich of the trigonometric ratios can we use? Which one of them has the two values\nthat we have and the one we need to determine? Our search narrows down to using\neither tan A or cot A, as these ratios involve AB and BC.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH109",
