      48.0,
      377.79,
      276.05,
      456.47
    ],
    "reading_order": 16,
    "text": "Solution : First let us draw a simple diagram to\nrepresent the problem (see Fig. 9.4). Here AB\nrepresents the tower, CB is the distance of the point\nfrom the tower and  ACB is the angle of elevation.\nWe need to determine the height of the tower, i.e.,\nAB. Also, ACB is a triangle, right-angled at B.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
